  <section class="mx-auto max-w-3xl px-6 py-16 sm:px-12">
    <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mb-6">PDF Processing Privacy</h2>
    <p class="mb-4">
      Unlike online PDF services that process your documents on remote servers, Toolix performs all PDF
      operations entirely within your browser. This means:
    </p>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6 space-y-2">
      <li>Your documents never touch a server</li>
      <li>No file size limits from upload restrictions</li>
      <li>Zero privacy risk for sensitive documents</li>
      <li>Works offline once assets are loaded</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Supported Operations</h3>
    <ul class="list-disc list-inside mb-6 space-y-2">
      <li><strong>Merge:</strong> Combine multiple PDFs into one document</li>
      <li><strong>Split:</strong> Extract specific pages from a PDF</li>
      <li><strong>Compress:</strong> Reduce PDF size by downsampling images and stripping metadata</li>
    </ul>
    <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mb-3">Frequently Asked Questions</h3>
    <div class="space-y-4">
      <div class="border-b pb-4">
        <h4 class="font-medium mb-2">Can I process password-protected PDFs?</h4>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          No. Password-protected PDFs require server-side decryption for security reasons. Our client-only
          architecture prevents this for user privacy protection.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-b pb-4">
        <h4 class="font-medium mb-2">What's the maximum file size?</h4>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          File size is limited by your device's memory. For typical documents (5-20 pages), processing
          is instantaneous. Larger files may take longer but remain private.
        </p>
      </div>
      <div class="border-b pb-4">
        <h4 class="font-medium mb-2">Does it work offline?</h4>
        <p class="text-[var(--color-text-secondary)]">
          Yes! Once the PDF library assets are loaded, all operations work completely offline thanks to
          PWA service worker caching.
        </p>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>
